and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Identifies important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about common technology. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Questions with Sentences / Asking for Clarification", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You ask for clarification when you want more details of what the other person is talking about. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We often ask for clarification when we are not clear on what the other person is referring to. We ask the other person to be more specific by giving more information. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use questions with sentences to ask for clarification. You ask a question including a sentence within the question, like <span class=\"italic\">Don't you think it sounds a bit too intense?</span><br/>Questions with sentences are called <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You can use <span class=\"strong\">embedded questions</span> like <span class=\"italic\">Can you tell me ... ?</span> or <span class=\"italic\">Do you know if/which/what ... ?</span> to ask for clarification. <br/>An <span class=\"strong\">embedded question</span> builds on a simple question.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:  <br/><span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">Simple question</span>: Where did you get that bagel? <span class=\"strong\"><br/>Embedded question</span>: Can you tell me where you got that bagel?</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Main Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Embedded Question\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you know ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Do you remember ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Can you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Could you tell me ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" what/where/when/who ... ?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Do you know what makes Montreal bagels so special?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Can you tell me where I can find these bagels then?", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Present Perfect vs. The Simple Past Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "<ol><li>We use the Present Perfect tense for actions which started in the past and are still happening now OR for finished actions which have a connection to the present.</li><li>We use the Simple Past tense for past events or actions which have no connection to the present.</li></ol>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Rule\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Explanation\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Present Perfect</span> is used when the time period has NOT finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">It's the best bagel I've ever had in town.</span> <br/> <span class=\\\"italic\\\">Have you tried these bagels?\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The time period goes up to the present.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"The <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Simple Past</span> is used when the time period HAS finished.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I had so many bagels the last time I was in New York!</span> <br/><span class=\\\"italic\\\"> I didn't eat any bagels when I was in New York.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" The trip to New York has finished.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bagel", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a round, baked pastry with a hole in the middle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: New York bagels are my favorite.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use in a conversation about  special food items.  ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "nothing comes close", "type": "name"}, {"content": "nothing else compares to it", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Nothing comes close to Montreal bagels.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "hands down", "type": "name"}, {"content": "without question", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The Montreal nightlife beats Boston's hands down.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to dip", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put something down briefly in liquid", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: They dip the bagels in honey before they bake them.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to boil", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to put something in a liquid that has reached boiling temperature (100 degrees Celsius)", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Then, they boil them for two minutes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "texture", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the feel and consistency of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: That's what gives the bagels their unique texture.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "bistro", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a type of French restaurant where food is served quickly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are many cute bistros in Montreal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "brewery", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place where beer is made commercially", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There are excellent breweries in Montreal.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "getaway", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a quick, usually improvised vacation", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sounds like the perfect getaway with Marco.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn7le01ob07re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think of 3 kinds of food that are typical of a country or a place.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Go on the Internet and find information about them.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a description (4 - \u00ad6 lines) about each one, including the country  or place of origin, how they are made, and explain why they are  popular.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your description aloud to your partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Ask questions about your partner's food description.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I talk about food, drink, and social activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask questions about food, drink, and social activities.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about people's experiences.", "type": "text"}]}]}